  {
   "@id": "https://w3id.org/ppp/lightnessRange/singleLightness",
   "@type": "skos:Concept",
   "inScheme": "https://w3id.org/ppp/",
   "skos:notation": "singleLightness",
   "prefLabel": {
    "fr": "éventail des clartés : une seule clarté",
    "en": "lightness range: single lightness"
   },
   "hiddenLabel": {
    "fr": "une seule clarté",
    "en": "single lightness"
   },
   "example": {
    "fr": "toute la zone a la même clarté (un mur peint uniformément, sous une lumière égale)",
    "en": "the whole area has the same lightness (an evenly painted wall, under even light)"
   },
   "regionOf": "https://w3id.org/ppp/lightnessRange",
   "broader": "https://w3id.org/ppp/lightnessRange"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://w3id.org/ppp/lightnessRange/closeLightnesses",
   "@type": "skos:Concept",
   "inScheme": "https://w3id.org/ppp/",
   "skos:notation": "closeLightnesses",
   "prefLabel": {
    "fr": "éventail des clartés : clartés proches",
    "en": "lightness range: close lightnesses"
   },
   "hiddenLabel": {
    "fr": "clartés proches",
    "en": "close lightnesses"
   },
   "example": {
    "fr": "des clartés un peu différentes, sans très clair ni très sombre côte à côte (un enduit nuageux, un lin chiné)",
    "en": "slightly different lightnesses, with nothing very light next to something very dark (a cloudy render, a mottled linen)"
   },
   "regionOf": "https://w3id.org/ppp/lightnessRange",
   "broader": "https://w3id.org/ppp/lightnessRange"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://w3id.org/ppp/lightnessRange/distantLightnesses",
   "@type": "skos:Concept",
   "inScheme": "https://w3id.org/ppp/",
   "skos:notation": "distantLightnesses",
   "prefLabel": {
    "fr": "éventail des clartés : clartés éloignées",
    "en": "lightness range: distant lightnesses"
   },
   "hiddenLabel": {
    "fr": "clartés éloignées",
    "en": "distant lightnesses"
   },
   "example": {
    "fr": "du très sombre et du très clair dans la même zone (un damier noir et blanc, une gravure en noir et blanc)",
    "en": "very dark and very light in the same area (a black-and-white chequerboard, a black-and-white engraving)"
   },
   "regionOf": "https://w3id.org/ppp/lightnessRange",
   "broader": "https://w3id.org/ppp/lightnessRange"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://w3id.org/ppp/subsurfaceDepth",
   "related": [
    "https://w3id.org/ppp/localIrregularity",
    "https://w3id.org/ppp/perceivedDepth",
    "https://w3id.org/ppp/surfaceGloss"
   ],
   "@type": "skos:Concept",
   "inScheme": "https://w3id.org/ppp/",
   "skos:notation": "subsurfaceDepth",
   "prefLabel": {
    "fr": "profondeur dans la matière",
    "en": "depth within the material"
   },
   "altLabel": {
    "en": "subsurface depth"
   },
   "definition": {
    "fr": "Degré auquel on a l’impression de voir dans l’épaisseur d’une matière, sous sa surface, de la matière où le regard s’arrête à la surface à celle où il paraît entrer loin.",
    "en": "The degree to which one has the impression of seeing into the thickness of a material, beneath its surface, from material where the gaze stops at the surface to material it seems to enter far."
   },
   "scopeNote": {
    "fr": [
     "Le regard s’arrête-t-il à la surface de cette matière, ou paraît-il entrer un peu, ou loin, dans son épaisseur ?",
     "Une vitre propre est transparente, mais on regarde à travers, vers ce qui est derrière : on ne voit pas d’épaisseur dans la vitre elle-même ; c’est ce qu’on voit à travers elle (transparence). Un paysage peint qui s’étage en plans relève de l’étagement en plans, pas d’une profondeur dans la matière."
    ],
    "en": [
     "Does the gaze stop at the surface of this material, or does it seem to go a little, or far, into its thickness?",
     "A clean window pane is transparent, but one looks through it, at what is behind: one sees no thickness in the pane itself; that is what one sees through it (transparency). A painted landscape receding in planes belongs to layering into planes, not to a depth within the material."
    ]
   },
   "note": {
    "fr": "candidat ; non éprouvé",
    "en": "candidate; untested"
   },
   "topConceptOf": "https://w3id.org/ppp/",
   "measurementState": "https://w3id.org/ppp/mesure/etat/methodes",
   "measurementSummary": {
    "fr": "En synthèse d’image, la diffusion de la lumière sous la surface se décrit par des propriétés optiques de la matière (coefficients de diffusion et d’absorption), qu’une technique de recherche mesure à partir d’images. C’est une mesure associée indirecte : elle sert à prédire l’aspect, pas à dire jusqu’où le regard paraît entrer ; elle n’est pas normalisée, et ne saisit ni l’observateur, ni l’éclairage de l’épisode, ni la distance.",
    "en": "In image synthesis, light scattering beneath the surface is described by optical properties of the material (scattering and absorption coefficients), which a research technique measures from images. It is an indirect associated measurement: it serves to predict appearance, not to say how far the gaze seems to go in; it is not standardised, and captures neither the observer, nor the lighting of the episode, nor the distance."
   },
   "measurementCaveat": {
    "fr": "Les régions de cette fiche restent perceptives : elles décrivent ce qu’un observateur voit, entend, sent ou touche dans les conditions déclarées. Une mesure associée peut éclairer une observation, mais elle ne définit pas les bornes des régions et ne remplace pas l’examen.",
    "en": "The regions of this entry remain perceptual: they describe what an observer sees, hears, smells or feels by touch under the declared conditions. An associated measurement can inform an observation, but it does not set the boundaries of the regions and does not replace examination."
   },
   "associatedMeasure": "https://w3id.org/ppp/subsurfaceDepth/mesure/jensen2001",
   "notRetainedMeasure": "https://w3id.org/ppp/subsurfaceDepth/mesure/non-retenue-1",
   "hasScale": "https://w3id.org/ppp/subsurfaceDepth/echelle",
   "narrower": [
    "https://w3id.org/ppp/subsurfaceDepth/atSurface",
    "https://w3id.org/ppp/subsurfaceDepth/slightlyInside",
    "https://w3id.org/ppp/subsurfaceDepth/farInside"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://w3id.org/ppp/localIrregularity/mesure/non-retenue-1",
   "@type": "ppp:NotRetainedMeasure",
   "rdfs_label": {
    "fr": "paramètres de rugosité de profil ou de surface (ISO 21920-2, ISO 25178-2)",
    "en": "profile or areal roughness parameters (ISO 21920-2, ISO 25178-2)"
   },
   "reason": {
    "fr": "ils résument le relief de toute une zone en une valeur moyenne ou extrême, sans repérer où la surface s’écarte de sa régularité d’ensemble ; ils ne valent pas pour un trait ou un bord, et ne saisissent ni la distance de vue, ni l’éclairage, ni l’observateur",
    "en": "they summarise the relief of a whole area in one mean or extreme value, without locating where the surface departs from its overall regularity; they do not apply to a line or an edge, and capture neither the viewing distance, nor the lighting, nor the observer"
   },
   "dct:bibliographicCitation": [
    "ISO 21920-2:2021. Geometrical product specifications (GPS) — Surface texture: Profile — Part 2: Terms, definitions and surface texture parameters. Genève : ISO.",
    "ISO 25178-2:2021. Geometrical product specifications (GPS) — Surface texture: Areal — Part 2: Terms, definitions and surface texture parameters. Genève : ISO."
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://w3id.org/ppp/localIrregularity/mesure/non-retenue-2",
   "@type": "ppp:NotRetainedMeasure",
   "rdfs_label": {
    "fr": "tolérances de bulles et d’inclusions du verre (ISO 10110-18, ISO 12543-6)",
    "en": "bubble and inclusion tolerances for glass (ISO 10110-18, ISO 12543-6)"
   },
   "reason": {
    "fr": "elles comptent des défauts par rapport à un verre sans bulle et ne disent pas où l’intérieur s’écarte de sa propre régularité ; la notation d’optique descend à des tailles invisibles à distance d’usage ; elles ne valent que pour le verre d’optique ou le verre feuilleté de bâtiment",
    "en": "they count defects against bubble-free glass and do not say where the interior departs from its own regularity; the optical notation goes down to sizes invisible at normal viewing distance; they apply only to optical glass or laminated building glass"
   },
   "dct:bibliographicCitation": [
    "ISO 10110-18:2018. Optics and photonics — Preparation of drawings for optical elements and systems — Part 18: Stress birefringence, bubbles and inclusions, homogeneity, and striae. Genève : ISO.",
    "ISO 12543-6:2021. Glass in building — Laminated glass and laminated safety glass — Part 6: Appearance. Genève : ISO."
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://w3id.org/ppp/localIrregularity/mesure/non-retenue-3",
   "@type": "ppp:NotRetainedMeasure",
   "rdfs_label": {
    "fr": "contrôle visuel des bulles et inclusions du verre d’optique (SCHOTT TIE-28 ; ISO 12123)",
    "en": "visual inspection of bubbles and inclusions in optical glass (SCHOTT TIE-28; ISO 12123)"
   },
   "reason": {
    "fr": "il compte bulles et inclusions par leur aire totale dans un volume donné, par rapport à un verre sans bulle, et ne traite leur concentration que comme un motif de rejet ; il ne dit pas l’écart perçu à la régularité propre de l’objet, ne vaut que pour le verre d’optique et ne saisit ni la distance de vue ni l’observateur",
    "en": "it counts bubbles and inclusions by their total area in a given volume, against bubble-free glass, and treats their concentration only as a ground for rejection; it does not state the perceived departure from the object’s own regularity, applies only to optical glass and captures neither the viewing distance nor the observer"
   },
   "dct:bibliographicCitation": [
    "SCHOTT (2016). TIE-28: Bubbles and Inclusions in Optical Glass. Technical Information, version de mai 2016. Mainz : SCHOTT.",
    "ISO 12123:2018. Optics and photonics — Specification of raw optical glass. Genève : ISO."
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://w3id.org/ppp/localIrregularity/echelle",
   "@type": "skos:OrderedCollection",
