   },
   "example": {
    "fr": "du grisé et du très vif dans la même zone (un fond gris semé de taches de couleur pure)",
    "en": "greyish and very vivid in the same area (a grey background scattered with patches of pure colour)"
   },
   "regionOf": "https://w3id.org/ppp/saturationRange",
   "broader": "https://w3id.org/ppp/saturationRange"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://w3id.org/ppp/scaleContrast/mesure/non-retenue-1",
   "@type": "ppp:NotRetainedMeasure",
   "rdfs_label": {
    "fr": "rapport des dimensions mesurées des deux éléments",
    "en": "ratio of the measured dimensions of the two elements"
   },
   "reason": {
    "fr": "la taille perçue d’un élément dépend de ce qui l’entoure (illusions de Delboeuf et d’Ebbinghaus) : un même rapport de dimensions peut donner des différences perçues différentes ; ne saisit ni la distance de vue, ni la disposition, ni l’observateur ; ISO 80000-3 définit la grandeur sans décrire de procédé de mesure",
    "en": "the perceived size of an element depends on what surrounds it (Delboeuf and Ebbinghaus illusions): the same ratio of dimensions can give different perceived differences; it captures neither the viewing distance, nor the layout, nor the observer; ISO 80000-3 defines the quantity without describing a measurement procedure"
   },
   "dct:bibliographicCitation": [
    "ISO 80000-3:2019. Quantities and units — Part 3: Space and time. Genève : ISO.",
    "Mruczek, R. E. B., Blair, C. D., Strother, L. & Caplovitz, G. P. (2017). Size Contrast and Assimilation in the Delboeuf and Ebbinghaus Illusions. In The Oxford Compendium of Visual Illusions (p. 262–268). New York : Oxford University Press."
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://w3id.org/ppp/scaleContrast/echelle",
   "@type": "skos:OrderedCollection",
   "prefLabel": {
    "fr": "échelle de « contraste d’échelle »",
    "en": "scale of “scale contrast”"
   },
